papers.abstract:
In this paper, we investigate dead-core problems for fully nonlinear degenerate parabolic equations with strong absorption, \begin{equation*}
  |Du|^{p} F(D^{2}u) - u_{t} = \lambda_{0}(x,t)\, u^{\mu}\, \chi_{\{u>0\}}(x,t)
  \qquad \text{in } \quad \Omega_{T} := \Omega \times (0,T), \end{equation*} where $0\le p<\infty$, $0<\mu<1$ and $u \geq 0 $ is a bounded viscosity solution satisfying $0\le u_t\le A_0u^\mu$ in the viscosity sense for some $0\le A_0<\infty$. We establish a sharp and improved parabolic $C^{\alpha}$-regularity estimate along the free boundary $\partial \{ u > 0 \}$, where \[ \alpha := \frac{2+p}{1+p-\mu} > 1 + \frac{1}{1+p}. \] Moreover, we establish weak geometric properties of solutions, such as non-degeneracy and uniform positive density. As an application, we obtain a Liouville-type theorem for entire solutions and gradient bounds. Finally, as a byproduct of our approach, we derive a new formulation of the gradient decay property and establish a Harnack-type inequality on time slices. It is worth noting that the results presented here extend those in da Silva {\em et al.}(Pacific J. Math., \textbf{300} (2019), 179--213) and (J. Differential Equations., \textbf{264} (2018), 7270--7293) to the degenerate setting, and can be viewed as a parabolic analogue of da Silva {\em et al.} (Math. Nachr., \textbf{294} (2021), 38--55) and Teixeira (Math. Ann., \textbf{364} (2016), 1121--1134).

In 2017, Keith defined and studied a multi-restricted partition function $RD^{l,t}(n)$, the number of integer partitions of n into parts that are simultaneously $l$-regular and $t$-distinct if none of the parts is divisible by $l$ and parts appear fewer than $t$ times. Thereafter, in a series of papers Buragohain et al. and Nadji et al. examined combinatorial and arithmetic properties of $RD^{l,t}(n)$. In this article, we focus on simultaneously $l$-regular and $t$-distinct partitions in 3-colors, $RD^{l,t}_3(n)$ and establish infinite families of congruences modulo powers of 3 for specific values of $(l,t)$. For instance, for positive integers $n$ and $k$, we have
  \begin{align*}
  \sum_{n=0}^{\infty}RD_3^{3,3}\left(3^kn+\frac{3^k+1}{2}\right)q^n\equiv0 \pmod{3^{k+1}}.
  \end{align*}
  Our approach involves Hirschhorn's H operator technique.

Given an integer $k \geq 2$, there are integers $M_k$ and $P_k$ so that for all $A \subseteq \mathbb F^n_p$ does not contain a restricted polynomial progression of the form
  \begin{align*}
  x, x+\begin{pmatrix}
  y_1 \\ y_2 \\ \vdots \\ y_n
  \end{pmatrix}, x+\begin{pmatrix}
  y_1^2 \\ y_2^2 \\ \vdots \\ y_n^2
  \end{pmatrix}, \ldots, x+\begin{pmatrix}
  y_1^{k-1} \\ y_2^{k-1} \\ \vdots \\ y_n^{k-1}
  \end{pmatrix},
  \end{align*}
  where $x \in \mathbb F^n_p$, with $p>P_k$, and $y \in \{0,2, 3, \ldots, M_k\}^n \backslash \{\vec{0} \}$, for some fixed $M_k$, then $A$ must have density bounded above by $\frac{C}{(\log^{(k^{O(k)})} n)^c}$, where $C, c>0$ only depend on $k$ and $p$. For $k\geq 4$, the best previously known bound came from the density Hales--Jewett theorem and was of inverse Ackermann type. The proof uses a recent inverse theorem for noise stability of Bhangale, Khot, Liu and Minzer, which arose in the study of constraint satisfaction problems. The main new ingredient is a proof that the underlying distribution counting restricted polynomial progressions does not admit a nontrivial abelian embedding, by way of an involved algebraic argument. Reasonable bounds are provided for $P_k$ and $M_k$.

In this paper, we focus on well-filtered spaces. By using the Rudin sets and WD sets, we obtain the following results:
  (1) The product of arbitrarily many Scott well-filtered dcpos is still well-filtered with respect to the Scott topology. Thus we give positive answers for two questions proposed by Xu and Zhao;
  (2) Let $P$ be a dcpo with $\Sigma K(P)$ being well-filtered and $Q$ an RB-domain. Then $\Sigma K(P\times Q)$ is well-filtered if $K(P\times Q)$ is a dcpo;
  (3) An intrinsic characterization of the $WD$ sets is given in terms of Scott open filters.
